  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of emergency Primary health care response to floods  affected communities in Baidoa district Bay region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtAccording to the 2023 HRP, less than one third of the people in floods -affected areas are estimated to have access to essential health care. Reported cholera cases continue to rise compared to recent years, while measles cases have spiked, particularly among children. ltbrgtThe project aims to provide life-saving emergency primary health care to 30,000(4000 men, 10,000 women, 8000 girls and 8000 girls) floods displaced areas and host communities in Baidoa district through one static and four mobile clinics through provision of maternal and neonatal and child Health Care as well as immunization to the target lt5gt, the project will also provide psychosocial and mental health service through the outreach and health facility&#xa0; as well as provide gender based violence mainstreaming within health projects, The project will also provide active community&#xa0; sensitization, mobilization , earlier warning as well as active referral services within the target location&#xa0; in Abagbedey, Buuli Gomor, Yaagey and Danooley&#xa0; &#xa0; outreach sites and one static MCH at ADC II in Baidoa district.&#xa0;ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
